#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:437
msgid "Command Line"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:439
msgid "UUIDs can be generated from the command line using `uuid`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:441
msgid ""
"$ npx uuid\n"
"ddeb27fb-d9a0-4624-be4d-4615062daed4\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:446
msgid ""
"The default is to generate version 4 UUIDS, however the other versions "
"are supported. Type `uuid --help` for details:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:448
msgid ""
"$ npx uuid --help\n"
"\n"
"Usage:\n"
"  uuid\n"
"  uuid v1\n"
"  uuid v3 <name> <namespace uuid>\n"
"  uuid v4\n"
"  uuid v5 <name> <namespace uuid>\n"
"  uuid v7\n"
"  uuid --help\n"
"\n"
"Note: <namespace uuid> may be \"URL\" or \"DNS\" to use the corresponding"
" UUIDs\n"
"defined by RFC9562\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:464
msgid "`options` Handling for Timestamp UUIDs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:466
msgid ""
"Prior to `uuid@11`, it was possible for `options` state to interfere with"
" the internal state used to ensure uniqueness of timestamp-based UUIDs "
"(the `v1()`, `v6()`, and `v7()` methods). Starting with `uuid@11`, this "
"issue has been addressed by using the presence of the `options` argument "
"as a flag to select between two possible behaviors:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:468
msgid "Without `options`: Internal state is utilized to improve UUID uniqueness."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:469
msgid ""
"With `options`: Internal state is **NOT** used and, instead, appropriate "
"defaults are applied as needed."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:471
msgid "Support"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:473
msgid ""
"**Browsers**: `uuid` [builds are "
"tested](/uuidjs/uuid/blob/main/wdio.conf.js) against the latest version "
"of desktop Chrome, Safari, Firefox, and Edge. Mobile versions of these "
"same browsers are expected to work but aren't currently tested."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:475
msgid ""
"**Node**: `uuid` [builds are "
"tested](https://github.com/uuidjs/uuid/blob/main/.github/workflows/ci.yml#L26-L27)"
" against node ([LTS releases](https://github.com/nodejs/Release)), plus "
"one prior. E.g. At the time of this writing `node@20` is the "
"\"maintenance\" release and `node@24` is the \"current\" release, so "
"`uuid` supports `node@18`-`node@24`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/node_modules/uuid/README.md:477
msgid ""
"**Typescript**: TS versions released within the past two years are "
"supported. "
"[source](https://github.com/microsoft/TypeScript/issues/49088#issuecomment-2468723715)"
msgstr ""

